p.src:
The next step is the central structural claim of the lecture: $\mathrm{human\ being}
\leftrightarrow
\mathrm{world}.$ The arrow does not mean simple mutual influence. Krishnamurti’s claim is stronger: the human being is the world, and the world is the human being. Human beings have made society through greed, anger, violence, pettiness, ambition, fear, and the search for security. At the same time, each human being is shaped by culture, tradition, language, and the social order into which he or she is born.

