p.src:
The lecture rejects the simple sequence $\mathrm{change\ environment}
\longrightarrow
\mathrm{change\ human\ being}.$ It also rejects the private opposite, as if a separate person first perfects himself and later affects society. The inward and outward are not two independent orders. In the lecture’s terms, $\mathrm{root\ change\ in\ the\ human\ being}
\longleftrightarrow
\mathrm{change\ in\ the\ world}.$

