p.src:
The problem can be written as an update rule: $\mathrm{encounter}_{n+1}
\longmapsto
\mathrm{interpretation}\bigl(\mathrm{encounter}_{n+1};\mathrm{memory}_{n}\bigr).$ The new encounter is translated through the old record. Krishnamurti’s point is exact: when the next experience is translated in terms of the old, it is never wholly new.

